# =============================================================================
# EcoVision Sentinel — what goes to GitHub
#
# Principle: the repository holds SOURCE and RESEARCH. It does not hold
# anything regenerable (builds, environments), anything huge and binary
# (model weights, the packaged .exe), or anything produced at runtime
# (logs, databases, screenshots).
#
# A fresh clone should let someone read the whole system and the whole
# thesis. It will NOT run until they add weights and run setup.bat --
# that is the intended trade: ~25 MB of repo instead of ~7 GB.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Dependencies & environments (regenerable) ------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.venv/
venv/
env/
# The bundled Python env shipped inside the installer -- 5.13 GB. It has its
# own internal .gitignore, but that alone is fragile (lost if the venv is ever
# regenerated wholesale), so the root file is authoritative too.
python-env/
python-env*/
.venv/
.venv*/

# ---- Build outputs (regenerable) --------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
# dist/ holds the 1.63 GB portable .exe. Ship it as a GitHub Release asset,
# never as a tracked file -- GitHub rejects blobs over 100 MB.
dist/
# dist_installer/ was the old separate Inno Setup output folder (retired
# once the installer's OutputDir moved to build alongside dist/'s own
# win-unpacked instead). This got missed once already: a build was
# committed here before this line existed and had to be stripped back out
# of history -- kept as dist_* below so any similarly-named build-output
# folder (dist_v2/, used to test a new installer without touching dist/'s
# current one, included) can never repeat that mistake.
dist_*/
*.egg-info/
pip-wheel-metadata/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---- Python bytecode ---------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ---- Secrets -- never commit -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
devteam_credentials.txt
devteamcredentials.txt

# ---- Model weights -----------------------------------------------------------
# The binaries stay out (11-72 MB each, ~400 MB total), but the sidecars and
# the README stay IN: they record input geometry, training manifest and
# measured test results for every checkpoint. That is the part a reader of
# the thesis actually needs, and it costs a few KB.
weights/**/*.pt
weights/**/*.pth
weights/**/*.onnx
weights/**/*.engine
weights/archive/
!weights/**/*.meta.json
!weights/README.md

# Stray model files anywhere else in the tree
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.task
!weights/**/*.meta.json

# ---- Runtime output ----------------------------------------------------------
logs/
data/
static/screenshots/
static/clips/
static/recordings/
runtime_ports.json
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
runs/
eval_report_val/
x3d_debug_out*/
Assault_Snapshots/
roboflow_cache/
yolo11n_openvino_model/
recordings
# ---- Superseded / scratch ----------------------------------------------------
archive/
useless/
requests/
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.orig
*.err
*.log
!docs/**/*.md

# ---- IDE / OS ----------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.vs/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.pytest_cache/
.cache/
.coverage

# =============================================================================
# EXPLICITLY KEPT — these were excluded by an earlier blanket rule
# =============================================================================
# docs/ used to be ignored wholesale, which meant the entire research record
# was absent from the repository. For a thesis project the reports ARE the
# deliverable, so they are tracked. Total ~25 MB.
!docs/
!docs/**

# ...EXCEPT docs/local-only/ -- deployment/ops docs with real network
# topology, hardware and site specifics for the actual pilot deployment.
# Was committed once (docs/deployment_plan.html, a512c4d) and purged from
# history with git-filter-repo on 2026-08-25 (it no longer appears in any
# commit) precisely because this kind of detail about a real, running
# public-safety camera system has no business being world-readable on a
# public GitHub repo. Anything in here stays local to whichever machine
# checked it out. Must come AFTER the !docs/** re-inclusion above -- git
# resolves conflicting patterns by last-match-wins, so this line ignores
# strictly this one subfolder without needing the broader docs/ carve-out
# to change at all.
docs/local-only/

# The app's own image assets. A blanket *.png rule previously excluded
# electron/logo.png, without which the installer builds with no icon and no
# masthead -- a clone could not reproduce the shipped UI.
!electron/logo.png
!build/icon.ico
!logo.png
!public/**

# Figures and animations belong to the research record.
!docs/figures/**
!docs/media/**

# =============================================================================
# Large media that is regenerable — excluded even inside docs/
# =============================================================================
# Rebuild with: .venv\Scripts\python.exe tools\make_explainer_gifs.py
# (conv_explainer.mp4 is the exception: the script that made it is missing
# from the repo, so it is kept.)
docs/media/_preview_*.png
docs/media/_chk.png

# Word/Office lock files -- created while a .docx is open, one per viewer,
# never meant to be committed (and conflicts if two people have it open).
~$*.doc*
~$*.xls*
~$*.ppt*

# Firmware -- NEVER commit. hardware/esp32_smartpole_tracker.ino hardcodes the
# deployment Wi-Fi SSID and password, and it was pushed to a PUBLIC repo on
# 2026-08-20 before that was noticed. History was rewritten to purge it; this
# entry is what stops it coming back. The file still lives locally and in
# D:\EcoVisionImagesTraining\_hardware_backup\ -- it is ignored, not deleted.
#
# If firmware ever needs to be version-controlled, strip the credentials into
# a gitignored secrets.h first and commit only the .ino that includes it.
hardware/
*.ino
